<p>There's just way too much detail and smaller parts for an otherwise straightly played article, as well as oddly tone-breaking sentences.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It has no nose or ears, but does have yellow eyes</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>This is by no means the hottest the entity can become</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm no science expert, but the description of certain aspects like the radiation (&quot;Time of day, ambient temperature and the composition of&#8230;&quot;) or the 'gravitational acceleration' it uses to eat seem a little silly. Other aspects, such as the expungment of procedures should it try to escape, and the 'agitated state' doesn't support the article's cause.</p>

